--- Data source bound to the generated C# client (P1/S8 ObservableObject ViewModel; ADR-004) ---
The manifest record classifies this page as "no API data sources — renders from navigation params /
local state" (no `data` parity items). The web page does perform exactly one read, so the native port
binds it through the generated contract client and renders the same loading/empty/error/success states:
  request('/vampire-drain/stats?vehicle_id=…')  GET /vampire-drain/stats  -> VampireDrainClientFeed.FetchAsync (op get_api_v1_vampire_drain_stats)
The page renders only dimensionless percentages, hours, a 0–100 score and the kWh value the web
contract already supplies, so there is NO SI quantity to convert; every value is formatted at the
VampireDrainProjection display boundary (web fmtNumber parity: a missing scalar reads as 0). The shell
registration mounts the page over EmptyVampireDrainFeed (the no-backend empty surface) until a DI host
wires the generated-client feed, exactly as the RegenEfficiency / EnergyProducts predecessors do.

Note (R-class honesty): the live GET /vampire-drain/stats handler currently returns a different rollup
shape (event_count, avg_drain_pct_per_day, …) than the web page's VampireDrainStats contract. The
native parser tolerates that exactly as the web page does — the object parses, the page-specific fields
read as zero and the nested arrays are empty, so the surface renders Success with zeroed cards and
empty charts (covered by test Stats_FromJson_defaults_missing_scalars_to_zero_for_the_backend_shape).
The web source is the parity contract (ADR-002/ADR-006); the native port mirrors it field-for-field.

